    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Riders With A Passenger Traffic Preparation</h1>
    <p>Hanoi traffic is not hostile, but it is conversational, and like any conversation it punishes people who join it without listening first. Riding two-up adds a second variable: every decision the rider makes is now transmitted through a passenger who feels it before they understand it. Preparation for that reality is not a riding course and it is not courage; it is a set of small habits built before the first intersection, so the first intersection is a rehearsal instead of a test.</p>
    <p>This page is the traffic chapter of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster written for riders carrying a passenger. The verified rental prices and periods live on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the machine itself should be chosen with the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-bike-choice/">bike-choice page for two-up riders</a> before any of the habits below matter.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Read the traffic before you join it</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The passenger briefing: five minutes that change everything</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Mounting, dismounting and the first hundred metres</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Positioning in the flow</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Intersections, roundabouts and the shoulder check</a></li>
